        "title": "06 - Phototypesetting: The Transitional Era (1950s–1980s)",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GENERATION 2 (1960s): Electro-optical\n  Electronic control of exposure timing + lens adjustment\n  CRT tubes beginning to appear for character generation\n  Speed: ~5,000–8,000 chars/hr\n  Examples: Linofilm, Photon 713, IBM 2680"
    },
